# .gitignore — Files to Exclude from Git
# ==========================================
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS:
#   Some files should NEVER be committed to git:
#   - .env → contains secrets (passwords, API keys)
#   - __pycache__ → Python's compiled bytecode cache (auto-generated)
#   - venv/envku/ → virtual environment (each developer installs their own)
#   - logs/ → log files are generated at runtime, not code
#
# HOW GIT USES THIS:
#   Git ignores any file/folder matching these patterns.
#   They won't appear in "git status" and can't be accidentally committed.

# ── Secrets & Config ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
*.env.local

# ── Python Cache ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/

# ── Virtual Environments ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
venv/
env/
.venv/
envku/
.env.bak

# ── Logs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
logs/*.log

# ── IDEs & Editors ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store

# ── Distribution / Packaging ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/
